A||||5||DavidHenshaw||SCCA Nationals at Mid--Ohio||||1||
Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||08-26-2001||10:39 PM||||Attended the Sports Car Club of America national finals at Mid-Ohio Raceway today. Many different types of cars, lots of good racing. Saw two fieros compete. The track is located near Lexington Ohio just south of Mansfield. Lots of nice places for fans to get a good view of on track action.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-27-2001||12:52 AM||||ya, I took new gf today for first 'date' shed never seen a car race live and loved it.<BR>my favorite spots are the little hill by tower where they come into uphill left hander and back down into the essess or the hairpin before they go down the backstretch.<BR>You ought to go to the Vintage Gran Prix next june and see all the 50's thru 70's cars racing. I hope a bunch of Fiero guys go next year and camp out, also huge car show in the infield.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||08-27-2001||09:07 AM||||Sounds like fun.  What classes were the Fieros competing in?  Were they street-based cars (like Improved Touring) or tube-framed (GT2)?<P>I'll be there for the Nationals next month, all three days.  It's the closest, most competitive road racing you'll see anywhere -- and it's only $30 for a weekend ticket.  That's only $1.25 a race!<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||HarryG||08-27-2001||12:15 PM||||Chad,<BR>Next month?<BR>Are you talking about the Valvoline Runoffs?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000004||ChadMan||08-27-2001||02:21 PM||||Yep -- I can't wait!  I have gone every year since they moved the Runoffs to Mid-Ohio.  I may catch hell for saying this, but I think the Runoffs is the most fun race I've ever been to.||||reg||14
Z||000005||DavidHenshaw||08-27-2001||04:49 PM||||The fieros were in the GT2 class. They did not appear to me to be tube frames but when the closest you can get is 50 feet and with the cars doing better than 50 in the tightest curves and a ton and a half in the straights you don't get an up close look. Very exciting to watch. <P>My favorite spot would be a toss up between the bank you mentioned in the ss's and the higher of the two grandstands across the track from that same bank.<P>Dave <P>86 GT||||reg||1
